 \begin{decision}[A process is unique and local]
-A process is one node, in one slot, running only on the device whose
-scheduler started it. Its node is ephemeral, so the graph keeps it in one
-slot (\code{one-place}) and never saves it. A node placed with \code{place},
-or brought from storage or from elsewhere, is not started, whatever it holds:
-only \code{start} starts, and each \code{start} that is not matched makes a
-new process. Another device may be sent the node, as presence
-(\code{PRESENCE.tex}), and read it, but never runs it. What a host starts
-when it boots is the host's own.
+One node, one slot, running only on the device whose scheduler started it.
+Ephemeral (\code{one-place}, never saved). Only \code{start} starts, each
+unmatched one making a new process; a node placed with \code{place}, or brought
+from storage or elsewhere, is not started, whatever it holds. Other devices
+may be sent the node, as presence (\code{PRESENCE.tex}), and read it; never
+run it. What a host starts at boot: its own.
 \end{decision}
 
